// Same touch-ally deviation as `barkskin.ron` in this folder: sheet range is
// Touch and the description is explicitly second-person-to-an-ally ("You
// touch a willing ally"), which `SelfBuff` cannot deliver (always lands on
// the caster). Uses the established touch-ally pattern instead (see
// `barkskin.ron`'s own comment for the citation trail).
// The sheet's real mechanic -- granting the target an entirely new usable
// cone-breath attack they can trigger repeatedly for the duration -- has no
// primitive anywhere in this compendium; every existing ability a character
// can use is fixed at character-build time (equipped tool/innate pool), and
// nothing grants a temporary new active ability via a buff. That rider is
// dropped as out of content-only scope. Kept branch: the "infuse with
// elemental power" flavor, modeled with `BuffKind::Flame` ("your attacks
// cause targets to receive the burning debuff"), the nearest existing
// "makes your attacks elemental" buff, at a moderate strength.
BasicMelee(
    energy_cost: 35.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    swing_duration: 0.1,
    hit_timing: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    melee_constructor: (
        kind: Stab(damage: 1, poise: 0, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
        range: 3.0,
        angle: 20.0,
        attack_effect: Some((
            Buff((
                kind: Flame,
                dur_secs: 60.0,
                strength: Value(0.15),
                chance: 1.0,
            )),
            AttackSource(Melee),
        )),
        attack_effect_target: Some(InGroup),
    ),
    meta: (
        school: Some(Transmutation),
        source: Some(Arcane),
        // level 2 spell -> min_level 12, same `level * 6` convention.
        requirements: (min_level: Some(12)),
    ),
)
